---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Betancur DS — Eliana Betancur" description="How I helped scale a siloed design system into an org-wide standard at UnitedHealthcare.">
  <div class="px-6 sm:px-10 pt-8 pb-20">
    <article class="w-full page-reveal">

      <!-- <nav class="mb-10">
        <a href="/" class="font-mono text-sm text-warmgray-500 hover:text-warmgray-800 transition-colors">← Back</a>
      </nav> -->

      <p class="font-mono font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rust-700 mb-5 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="inline-block w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-rust-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Case Study — Design Systems
      </p>

      <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.1] mb-6">
        Betancur DS
      </h1>

      <p class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-12">
        How I helped turn a fragmented, low-adoption design system into an org-wide standard at UnitedHealthcare through documentation, accessibility, and engineering partnership.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-16 py-8 border-t border-b border-warmgray-300">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Role</p>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">UX Engineer</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Company</p>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">UnitedHealthcare</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Timeline</p>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">2022 – 2026</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-warmgray-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Tools</p>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 font-medium">Figma, React, Storybook</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4">The problem</h2>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When I joined UnitedHealthcare, the design system existed in name only. Individual product teams had built their own component libraries, their own patterns, their own conventions with no shared source of truth.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The same UI problems were being solved six different ways across six different teams. Design-to-engineering handoffs were inconsistent and slow. Accessibility was treated as a retrofit if it was treated at all. And engineers were not using the system because it was not built with them in mind.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed">
          The core issue was not the components. It was that the system had no foundation anyone could trust or build on.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4">Where I started</h2>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          I started by building components, getting hands-on with what existed and understanding where the gaps were. The problems were not technical, they were structural. No contribution process, no usable documentation, no clear path for an engineer from needing a component to using the right one.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed">
          Once that was clear, my focus shifted from building components to building the system around them. The things that would make adoption possible and sustainable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-6">What I did</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Documentation</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed">
              I researched how leading design systems document their work and built documentation covering component usage, token architecture, and contribution guidelines, making the system self-service so engineers did not need to ask a designer every time they needed a component.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Accessibility</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed">
              I worked closely with the accessibility team to lead a WCAG 2.1 AA compliance initiative across the full component library. Every component got documented keyboard behavior, ARIA patterns, and contrast requirements.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Engineering handoff</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed">
              I helped establish a formal handoff process with clear specs, token references, and interaction states documented before anything was handed off. What got designed was what got built.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warmgray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Org-wide adoption</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-800 leading-relaxed">
              The system grew from something one team used to something adopted across the organization. Documentation and process made adoption a natural outcome rather than a mandate.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4">What I learned</h2>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          A design system is not a component library. The work that makes a system scale is invisible. The documentation, the processes, the relationships with engineers and accessibility specialists who make it real.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed">
          The most important skill I developed was not designing components. It was making the system easy for other people to use, contribute to, and trust.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-800 mb-4">Betancur DS — the artifact</h2>
        <p class="font-sans text-base text-warmgray-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Betancur DS is a personal design system built to demonstrate the principles developed during four years at UHC. Token architecture, accessibility-first components, and documentation structure.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-warmgray-800 rounded-lg p-8 relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute -right-8 -top-8 w-48 h-48 rounded-full border border-warmgray-700 opacity-20"></div>
          <div class="absolute right-8 top-8 w-28 h-28 rounded-full border border-warmgray-700 opacity-10"></div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-rust-200 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Betancur DS — Official Library</p>
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-warmgray-100 mb-3">Design Systems</h3>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-warmgray-500 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Color tokens, spacing, typography, elevation, and 14 components and growing.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-warmgray-700 text-warmgray-500">Token architecture</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-warmgray-700 text-warmgray-500">WCAG 2.1 AA</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-warmgray-700 text-warmgray-500">14 components</span>
          </div>
          <a
            href="https://www.figma.com/design/U49gXIbwVYqFNFQnUIWLqv/Eliana-Betancur---DS?node-id=91-4755"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-mono text-sm text-rust-300 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-rust-200 transition-colors"
          >
            View in Figma →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="pt-0">
        <a href="/" class="font-mono text-sm text-warmgray-500 hover:text-warmgray-800 transition-colors">← Back to home</a>
      </div>

    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-reveal {
    animation: rise 0.6s ease-out both;
  }
  @keyframes rise {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .page-reveal { animation: none; }
  }
</style>